    "https://career.kzoo.edu/": {
      "title": "Center for Career and Professional Development",
      "description": "Center for Career and Professional Development –  | Kalamazoo College Skip to main content quicklinks ▼ ✗ Academic admin council Academic calendar Academic stds committee Accessiblity at K Admission Advising African studies Alcohol & other drugs Alumni engagement American studies Anthropology/sociology Arabic Arboretum Archives Arcus center Art Hornet sports Athletic training Biology Biology & chem center Bookstore BrandK Business office Campus event calendar Campus safety Career & professional dev Careers in health Catalog Cauldron Ctr for civic engagement Ctr for international pgrms Chemistry & Biochemistry Chinese Classics College communication Community & global health Community council Complex systems studies Commencement Computer science Copyright Counseling Crisis response Critical ethnic studies Critical theory Development Dining services Directories Disability services Diversity, equity, inclusion Donor relations East Asian studies Economics & business Educational policies committee Engineering Environmental stewardship Environmental studies English Experiential education committee Facilities management Facilities reservations Faculty development committee Faculty executive committee Faculty grants Faculty personnel committee Fellowships and grants Festival playhouse Film & media studies Financial aid First year experience Fitness wellness center French Gardens & growing spaces German Global crossroads Health center Health science Jewish studies History Hornet hive Hornet HQ Human resources Humanities Integrated Locational Learning Inclusive excellence Index (student newspaper) Information services Institutional assessment Institutional research Institutional review board Intercultural student life International area studies International programs Intramural sports Japanese KCCSR Council of student reps LandSea Learning commons Learning support Lgbtqai+ student resources Library Mail & copy center Math Math/physics center Microsoft Stream Microsoft Teams Mobile app Moodle Music OneDrive Outdoor programs Parents' resources Payroll Phi Beta Kappa Philharmonia Philosophy Physics Physical education Political science Pre-law advising Provost Psychology Public policy urban affairs Recycling Registrar Religion Religious & spiritual life Research Guides (libguides) Residential life Safety (security) Sexual safety Shared passages program SharePoint online Sophomore experience Spanish Strategic plan Student accounts Student development Student activities Student organizations Study abroad Support staff Sustainability Teaching & learning committee Teaching commons Theatre arts Title IX Webmail Women, gender, sexuality Writing center About K K-Plan Academics Admission Alumni GIVE News Life at K Athletics APPLY Close Navigation Center for Career and Professional Development Home Students Explore Your Path Beyond K Families All Student Resources Employers On-Campus Employers Employer Resources Alumni Faculty/Advisors Advisor Playbook Faculty Resources Impact Home What can we help you find? Search Search The CCPD is here to support you as you: CONSIDER your values, strengths, and interests as you build your K-Plan and plan for Life after K. COMMUNICATE your knowledge, skills and experiences effectively verbally, in writing and online to access career opportunities. CONNECT with employers, alumni and other professionals to explore interest areas and test out career options. Start your journey by dropping by the Career Studio . Or begin by checking out our Resources . Latest News: See What We Built Together: CCPD’s 2025–26 Impact Report Inside a Photographic Archive in Rome Learning Beyond the Classroom: A Student-Led Day in Lansing What our Alumni Tell Us Reflection to Direction: Supporting Sophomores as They Explore What Comes Next Graduate School Fair Recap Upcoming Events: See a full list of upcoming events in Handshake . Wednesday September 30 @ 3:00 - 5:00 pm . Dewing Commons Employer Connection Fair Wednesday October 7 @ 11:00 am - 1:00 pm . TBD Career Studio Takeover – University of Michigan Ross School of Business Wednesday January 20 @ 3:00 - 5:00 pm . Dewing Commons Employer Connection Fair Access Online, 24/7: Handshake : Search for on-campus and off-campus jobs, register for events, or schedule a 1:1 appointment with a career coach. Career Connection Toolkit : Access a growing collection of online modules at your own pace. Learn how to create a basic resume, tailor it for specific opportunities, and connect with alumni for career exploration and mentorship. PathwayU : Utilize this online predictive guidance platform to connect to your greatest sense of purpose as you make choices throughout your education, career, and employment journey. KConnect : Connect with alumni and students on Kalamazoo College’s official networking platform to get career advice, mentorship, and job leads. Big Interview & Big Resume : Practice interview skills and get instant feedback on your resume using these online tools. What can I do with this major? : Explore career paths linked to every K major and find resources to plan your next steps. Forage : Complete free job simulations designed by employers to gain experience without applying or interviewing. Updated August 19, 2026 by Rachel Wood Contact CCPD 269.337.7183 Career@kzoo.edu About Us Meet the CCPD Staff! Meet the CCPD Pets! Our Mission News Address Dewing Hall 1200 Academy St Kalamazoo, MI 49006 Social Media Instagram YouTube Contact Info Kalamazoo College 1200 Academy Street Kalamazoo, Michigan 49006-3295 USA Information 269.337.7000 Admission 800.253.3602 Contact List Directories Search this site Sitemap Map and Directions Academic Calendars Employment Departments and Programs Library Registrar Bookstore For Parents Crisis Response Nondiscrimination Policy Title IX Bias Reporting Consumer Information Web Accessibility Policy Privacy Policy Official Disclaimer © Kalamazoo College All Rights Reserved 2018"
    },
    "https://careersinhealth.kzoo.edu/": {
      "title": "Careers in Health",
      "description": "Careers in Health –  | Kalamazoo College Skip to main content quicklinks ▼ ✗ Academic admin council Academic calendar Academic stds committee Accessiblity at K Admission Advising African studies Alcohol & other drugs Alumni engagement American studies Anthropology/sociology Arabic Arboretum Archives Arcus center Art Hornet sports Athletic training Biology Biology & chem center Bookstore BrandK Business office Campus event calendar Campus safety Career & professional dev Careers in health Catalog Cauldron Ctr for civic engagement Ctr for international pgrms Chemistry & Biochemistry Chinese Classics College communication Community & global health Community council Complex systems studies Commencement Computer science Copyright Counseling Crisis response Critical ethnic studies Critical theory Development Dining services Directories Disability services Diversity, equity, inclusion Donor relations East Asian studies Economics & business Educational policies committee Engineering Environmental stewardship Environmental studies English Experiential education committee Facilities management Facilities reservations Faculty development committee Faculty executive committee Faculty grants Faculty personnel committee Fellowships and grants Festival playhouse Film & media studies Financial aid First year experience Fitness wellness center French Gardens & growing spaces German Global crossroads Health center Health science Jewish studies History Hornet hive Hornet HQ Human resources Humanities Integrated Locational Learning Inclusive excellence Index (student newspaper) Information services Institutional assessment Institutional research Institutional review board Intercultural student life International area studies International programs Intramural sports Japanese KCCSR Council of student reps LandSea Learning commons Learning support Lgbtqai+ student resources Library Mail & copy center Math Math/physics center Microsoft Stream Microsoft Teams Mobile app Moodle Music OneDrive Outdoor programs Parents' resources Payroll Phi Beta Kappa Philharmonia Philosophy Physics Physical education Political science Pre-law advising Provost Psychology Public policy urban affairs Recycling Registrar Religion Religious & spiritual life Research Guides (libguides) Residential life Safety (security) Sexual safety Shared passages program SharePoint online Sophomore experience Spanish Strategic plan Student accounts Student development Student activities Student organizations Study abroad Support staff Sustainability Teaching & learning committee Teaching commons Theatre arts Title IX Webmail Women, gender, sexuality Writing center About K K-Plan Academics Admission Alumni GIVE News Life at K Athletics APPLY Close Navigation Careers in Health HOME EXPLORE CHIROPRACTIC DENTISTRY MEDICINE NURSING OCCUPATIONAL THERAPY OPTOMETRY PHARMACY PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT PHYSICAL THERAPY PUBLIC HEALTH VETERINARY MEDICINE PREPARE ACADEMICS CLINICAL SERVICE RESEARCH APPLY APP PREP PROGRAM APP PREP PROGRAM NEW APPLICANTS APP PREP PROGRAM CONTINUING APPLICANTS APP PREP PROGRAM REAPPLICANTS LETTER COLLECTION SERVICE (2026) GUIDELINES FOR LETTER WRITERS LETTER OF RECOMMENDATION STATEMENTS LETTERS INTERVIEWS GROWTH YEAR Contact HOME Kalamazoo College’s Careers in Health and Medicine office assists and supports students as they explore health and medicine graduate and professional programs. Individuals interested in pursuing careers in these areas are encouraged to examine this website to determine the necessary prerequisites and application timeline as well as meet with the director to consider strengths and areas for opportunity, reflect on readiness to apply, and navigate the application process. The Careers in Health and Medicine office supports students and alumni until they are ready to apply to their chosen graduate and/or professional program. During the year this office offers: Pre-health sessions and workshops that provide opportunities to help students explore health careers, learn about holistic development, hear tips on becoming a competitive applicant, and prepare for the application cycle. 2025 – 2026 PRE-HEALTH SESSIONS & WORKSHOPS TIMELINE E.P.I.C: BECOME A COMPETITIVE APPLICANT APP PREP PROGRAM One-on-one advising sessions where students : are connected with the appropriate resources, can explore careers in healthcare, can determine the right courses to take, and discuss how to find meaningful academic and extracurricular activities. SCHEDULE AN ADVISING APPOINTMENT HEALTH AND MEDICINE STUDENT ORGANIZATIONS CAREERS IN HEALTH AND MEDICINE GOALS EXPLORE Assist students in exploring various careers in health and medicine to determine the right fit through programs, advising, and reflection. PREPARE Help students to determine readiness to apply by having them reflect on their experiences and competencies. APPLY Support students and provide resources as they apply to their chosen professional or graduate program. ABOUT CAREERS IN HEALTH AND MEDICINE VISION : To demonstrate the highest standards of service to students and alumni in holistic planning towards a career in health and medicine and encouraging self-reflection regarding competencies needed for professionals in these fields. The office aims to enhance collaborations with faculty, alumni, graduate and professional schools, as well as service and health related organizations to prepare future health and medicine professionals. MISSION : To provide programs and guidance with the highest standards of service for Kalamazoo College students and alumni. The office provides a supportive environment where students and alumni are encouraged to thrive academically and recognize how their academics and co-curricular activities such as research, service and clinical interactions translate to careers in health and medicine. The mission of the Careers in Health and Medicine office supports the overall values of Kalamazoo College. Particularly the components of the liberal arts education embodied in the K-Plan , which nurtures careers in health and medicine through an academically rigorous interdisciplinary curriculum encouraging scientific exploration, humanistic inquiry, and experiential opportunities. WHO WE SERVE : The Careers in Health and Medicine office serves undergraduates and alumni of Kalamazoo College who are seeking careers in health and medicine. This office is a resource throughout a student’s undergraduate career, providing information about course selection, volunteer involvement, health related experiences as well as exploring growth year opportunities. Undergraduates and alumni who are pursuing careers in health and medicine have access to all of the services provided by this office, but those applying to professions other than medicine and dentistry (e.g., nursing, veterinary medicine, pharmacy, and public health) do not require a Health Sciences Advisory Committee Letter. Updated August 19, 2026 by Jessica Fowle Contact Info Kalamazoo College 1200 Academy Street Kalamazoo, Michigan 49006-3295 USA Information 269.337.7000 Admission 800.253.3602 Contact List Directories Search this site Sitemap Map and Directions Academic Calendars Employment Departments and Programs Library Registrar Bookstore For Parents Crisis Response Nondiscrimination Policy Title IX Bias Reporting Consumer Information Web Accessibility Policy Privacy Policy Official Disclaimer © Kalamazoo College All Rights Reserved 2018"
    },
